ure, called on demand and never stored: an implicit graph (Boost’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"grid_graph"},{"type":"text","text":", LEMON’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GridGraph"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FullGraph"},{"type":"text","text":"). It is a lawful "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":", so every generic algorithm runs"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on it, including those that need the whole vertex set (components, centrality), with no edge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"storage."}],"title":"ImplicitDirectedGraph","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ImplicitDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ImplicitDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph","type":"topic"},"doc://ImplicitGraphs/documentation/ImplicitGraphs/ImplicitDirectedGraph/Successors":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/Successors","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"ImplicitDirectedGraph.Successors","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Successors"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The closure’s row for one vertex, each target checked to be a vertex as it is read (not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when the row is formed). A struct rather than a lazy map, so an algorithm that keeps an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"iterator per vertex on its stack (Tarjan’s) allocates nothing for it."}],"url":"\/documentation\/implicitgraphs\/implicitdirectedgraph\/successors","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Successors"}]},"doc://ImplicitGraphs/documentation/ImplicitGraphs":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Implici